# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Grimoire .gitignore
#
# ONE HARD RULE, enforced by lint rule L8: this file must never ignore a *.md
# path. All durable state in this system is markdown. If a tool ever needs a
# non-markdown file to hold state, that is a bug, not a config change.
# `bin/g-lint` fails the build if any line here would ignore markdown.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Verbatim source material. Copyrighted books, papers, articles, PDFs.
# A `source` note records provenance; the raw bytes stay here, on your disk.
# This is the ONLY thing this repo refuses to track.
raw/

# A README placed inside a raw/ directory is ours, not the source's.
!**/raw/README.md

# Private scratch. Your own `self/` is deliberately NOT ignored: your own prior
# reasoning is durable state and belongs in git. See docs/DESIGN-DECISIONS.md.

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# App state (Obsidian is supported as a *reader*, never as a dependency)
.obsidian/
.trash/
workspace.json

# Binary artefacts — never durable state
*.pdf
*.epub
*.apkg
*.zip
*.tar.gz

# Tooling noise
node_modules/
.venv/
__pycache__/

# Linter scratch space
.omo-scratch/
